From 76c32e1176b03c46e39ec2470d34f51dc22900d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 04:20:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show a dialog's content when it is wrapped to scroll

A modal dialog whose custom content scrolls could open with only its
title and buttons. Whether the scrolling container shows is worked out
from the wrap setting, but changing that setting did not work it out
again; it waited for some later property to do so. The binder applies
properties in no fixed order, so when the wrap setting came last the
container stayed hidden. That hid the risk sentence and the permission
list in the dialog that adds an extension, on some devices and not
others.

Changing the wrap setting now updates what is shown, as every other
setter does.
---
 .../components/browser_ui/modaldialog/ModalDialogView.java   | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/components/browser_ui/modaldialog/android/java/src/org/chromium/components/browser_ui/modaldialog/ModalDialogView.java b/components/browser_ui/modaldialog/android/java/src/org/chromium/components/browser_ui/modaldialog/ModalDialogView.java
index dffd2393671..dcb5197f7bd 100644
--- a/components/browser_ui/modaldialog/android/java/src/org/chromium/components/browser_ui/modaldialog/ModalDialogView.java
+++ b/components/browser_ui/modaldialog/android/java/src/org/chromium/components/browser_ui/modaldialog/ModalDialogView.java
@@ -480,6 +480,11 @@ public class ModalDialogView extends BoundedLinearLayout implements View.OnClick
             mCustomViewContainer.addView(view);
         }
         mCustomViewContainer.setVisibility(wasVisible);
+        // Bare: whether the scroll view shows depends on this setting, and nothing
+        // else recalculates it if this is the last property the binder applies.
+        // The binder's order is not fixed, so without this a dialog could show
+        // its title and buttons with its content hidden.
+        updateContentVisibility();
     }
 
